  "reviewed_semantics": [
    "The common supported prior conditions the public two-Gaussian mixture as a whole in the original entering x base measure; its common normalizer cancels only in the specified cost contrasts.",
    "The entering map uses u0=H*h0 with both product derivatives, removes legacy coordinate scales before full joint Gram mapping, and transports the full entering derivative factor forward to endpoint coordinates.",
    "Both anchors and every audit candidate must pass the full strict entering/path support check using prefix charge extrema including zero; no clipping or arithmetic allowance admits an invalid point.",
    "The mixture prior Hessian includes the negative responsibility-covariance term. Full joint correlations remain present; no single-Gaussian substitution, curvature clipping or covariance pseudoinverse is used.",
    "Actual combined objective/gradient evaluations, Hessian-triggered work and final verification share each1024-evaluation cap; each arm has one start and at most100 iterations. There is no model evaluation inside either surrogate/prior solve.",
    "Finite strictly feasible KKT-unresolved candidates receive their already-budgeted audit passes. Raw optimizer success never promotes an independently unresolved solve.",
    "Acceptance compares the identical-prior computed nonlinear costs with the frozen summand-resolution allowance, and is labeled accepted_feasible_point_improvement. It does not require both solves to converge and does not imply a MAP or global optimum.",
    "The accumulation/combination allowance does not certify model recurrence, libm, residual/J products or prior-density evaluation against exact real arithmetic.",
    "Generation replacement retains exactly one active likelihood block for source:[0,252000), with one prior and unchanged observation cursor. Old and replacement evidence are never added.",
    "The execution contract, immutable reviewed-source map, committed source objects, executable/runtime receipt, original observations and historical metadata are checked before launch and rehashed during the sequence.",
    "Exclusive per-solve started/result/exception files retain partial work. Started model passes have unknown counts until a valid attempted-step count is recovered; no failed or interrupted attempt authorizes a retry.",
    "Failure-only bounded emergency result/receipt closure preserves evidence after an output-cap breach without claiming success. Final resource rollback restores generation0 ownership consistently.",
    "The outer observer launches the canonical supervisor once, closes full wait4 CPU/wall/RSS accounting, and checks combined attempt/observer bytes including its receipt. Failed outer closure vetoes reporting.",
    "Reporting verifies both inner and outer closure before any truth access, allows exactly two post-inference prior-algebra evaluations, and decodes at most one hash-verified endpoint truth record after inference.",
    "PD/interior inverse-curvature matrices are local shape diagnostics only, including at unresolved points. The audit Gram plus prior Hessian is a Gauss-Newton approximation, not the full nonlinear likelihood Hessian. No candidate-centered intervals or truth-in-interval tests are produced."
  ],
